-- title:
--   Mod-7 formal JTP products and theta series: $(q^r;q^7)$ and $H(q^7)$, $K(q^7)$
-- statement:
--   This bundle defines the mod-7 residue factor $1-q^{k+7n}$ and several mod-7 triple products with their per-$n$ factors, the theta exponents and coefficients of the associated bilateral series, the theta series and their analytic (complex) and formal-multilinear versions. It specifically defines Hirschhorn's $H(q^7)=(q^{21},q^{28},q^{49};q^{49})_\infty$ and $K(q^7)=(q^7,q^{42},q^{49};q^{49})_\infty$ together with their theta-series sides $\sum(-1)^kX^{(49k^2-7k)/2}$ and $\sum(-1)^kX^{(49k^2-35k)/2}$.
--
--   For arbitrary integer $c$, the coefficient function sums only over $|k|\le n+1$ with $((k(7k-c)/2).\mathrm{toNat})=n$. The validity predicate is $c\in\{1,3,5\}$; identifications with unrestricted bilateral series use this condition. The complex sums and products are totalized, with respective defaults $0$ and $1$ when summability or multipliability fails.
